abstract: >-
  A researcher-constructed corpus and methodological record for the study of
  ghost stories circulating in British, Irish, colonial, translated, and
  anthology-mediated print contexts from 1764 to 1913. Version 0.3 contains
  318 active textual witnesses after duplicate and alternate-translation
  review. The repository emphasizes corpus genealogy, selection decisions,
  provenance, uncertainty, textual integrity, and reproducibility.
